# Example denylist for scripts/public-safety-scan.sh. Placeholder terms only.
#
# The real list belongs to the consuming project and is kept OUTSIDE this repository, for example
# in that project's private repository. Point the scan at it with RQACI_DENYLIST=/path/to/list or
# `git config rqaci.denylist /path/to/list`; in CI, store its content in the RQACI_DENYLIST
# repository secret. The scan refuses a denylist inside this repository and an empty one.
#
# One extended regular expression per line, matched case-insensitively. Blank lines and lines
# starting with '#' are ignored. Findings report the line number, never the term.

# Product, company and repository names
example[ _-]?product
example-org/private-repo

# Internal hostnames, paths and identifiers
internal\.example\.com
/srv/example-workspace/
\bTICKET-[0-9]+\b
